cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use TACET, please cite the preprint below."
title: "Cost-Amortised Reasoning via Self-Distilling Neuro-Symbolic Cascades: From Knowledge-Graph QA to Regulatory-Compliance Checking"
authors:
  - family-names: "Nguyen"
    given-names: "Quang Minh"
    email: "quangminh2402.dev@gmail.com"
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"  # add once registered
abstract: >-
  TACET is a self-distilling neuro-symbolic cascade that amortises LLM cost in
  knowledge-graph question answering. Each query is routed through a sound
  forward-chaining Datalog rule engine, a confidence-calibrated ComplEx link
  predictor verified against a typed ontology, and an LLM teacher; an online
  distillation loop mines the teacher's answers into Datalog-checkable Horn
  rules and writes facts back, so the routing distribution drifts toward the
  cheap tiers as the workload streams. The measured dollar saving is delivered
  by answer reuse, while rule distillation is shown to be teacher-quality-gated.
  Tier-1 answers carry replayable proof trees with an ontology-preservation
  guarantee.
keywords:
  - neuro-symbolic
  - knowledge-graph
  - kgqa
  - datalog
  - proof-trees
  - rule-distillation
  - llm-cascade
  - cost-amortization
  - complex-embedding
